From 64f228ab03899dbefe6373ebca1f675749404965 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: 2026-10-14T02:08:53Z
Subject: HID: nanosic: align piano bridge and accessory power with panel blanking


Follow the DRM panel using the same API as nt36532e-thp. Blanking sends
0x25=0 before asserting sleep; unblanking releases sleep, waits for data
IRQ readiness, reads and dispatches pending frames through the normal
receive path, then sends 0x25=1 and restores LEDs/backlight. Attach while
blanked records presence without waking the accessory. Preserve HID,
protocol parsing, authentication, accelerometer and hinge interfaces.

Stock OS3.0.303.0.WPYCNXM nanosic_driver.ko evidence (text offsets):
- keyboard_early_suspend_work 0x6d10/0x6d38: 66-byte 0x25=0, checksum 0x5d.
- keyboard_suspend_work 0x6ed4-0x6ee8: panel off, GPIO_sleep(0), pm_relax.
- keyboard_early_resume_work 0x6914-0x6928: panel on, GPIO_sleep(1), then
  Nanosic_i2c_read_handler, which calls Nanosic_PM_try_wakeup at 0x91f0.
- PM_try_wakeup 0xfbc8-0xfc94: release TLMM3, test TLMM97 raw high. If
  already high no delay. Otherwise 0xfcb8-0xfd40 counts 99..0, each
  __const_udelay(0x418958) = 1000 us (ARM64 UDELAY_MULT=4295); after high
  0xffd4-0xffdc uses 0x147aeb8 = 5000 us. Thus use a 100 ms ready limit
  and 5 ms settling only after waiting, with no reset/reload on timeout.
- keyboard_resume_work 0x6b3c/0x6b60: 66-byte 0x25=1, checksum 0x5e.

Use the existing empty-frame parser to drain, instead of discarding the
first IRQ as a resume token. System suspend synchronizes receive, runs
the same sleep sequence if needed, and gates all command/read producers
before the I2C parent can suspend. Resume only clears that gate; a panel
enable delivered before bus resume is completed by one freezable work
item. A resume without a panel-enable event sends no piano commands.

Delete the community 25 ms resume delay, first-IRQ drop, blind reset and
firmware reload, and suspend's unexplained 10 ms delay. The stock reset
fallback is deliberately not reproduced. Timeout is an explicit error.
No periodic work, retry, additional power owner or userspace dependency.

Data GPIO high also occurs at idle; it is readiness, not a FIFO count.
Draining until the protocol's empty frame and the panel/system callback
integration are conservative standard-kernel choices, 待真机确认. The
accessory-side HID failure's prevention still needs hardware acceptance.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

